You may use, copy, modify, and run the Software privately, including
for personal, educational, and internal use. You may redistribute the
Software and modified versions, and you may run a public deployment,
only if you comply with sections 2, 3, and 4 and the deployment is not
a commercial service.

2. No commercial service
You may not use the Software, or a modified or derivative version, to
provide a commercial service. A commercial service means offering the
Software's world, client, or backend to third parties for a fee,
subscription, advertising, sponsorship, or other commercial advantage.

A copy with a different name, region, text, or branding is still
subject to this section when it contains a substantial part of the
Software.

You may not sell, license, or otherwise commercially exploit the
Original Assets on their own or as part of another product.

This section does not limit 김도훈 (CrazyLabs) from operating or
licensing the Software, including as a commercial service.

3. Attribution
The copyright notice and this license must stay with every copy or
substantial portion of the Software.

A public deployment or derivative work must keep visible attribution
to "CrazyLabs (https://crazylabs.co.kr)" and "Bumpinto World
(https://bumpinto.world)" in the user interface, including the world
gate badge and the bottom attribution bar.

